WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.980
This is a work of fiction based on research into the period in which it is set. The people,
 organization, laws, and names that appear in it have no relation to any in the real world.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.240
Taisho 12 (1923)
Siberia

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.900
Be...

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.020
Behind... you.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.080
Till Death Do Us Part

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.350
There you are, Colonel.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.650
A vamp?

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.400
In Kayabacho.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.270
Any vamp incidents in that area?

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.270
None confirmed.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:00.980
Check if anyone has moved into the area.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.730
You mean that the vamp is hiding in the area?

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:08.730
If it's hunting in unfamiliar territory,
it should be nearby.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:11.230
Mobilize the whole unit to search.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:13.060
Even them?

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:18.900
Of course.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.310
Chief!

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.730
This is real news!

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:27.270
People are burning up!
Human combustion at Tokyo Station!

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:28.810
There are witnesses!

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:33.350
You nincompoop, this paper doesn't
run ghost stories like that.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:36.980
Most of our readers are modern girls! Flappers!

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:42.810
What about that Imperial Theater
actress's suspected elopement?

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.400
Oh, yeah! Misaki, who played Salomé!

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.900
I really liked her!

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.900
I can't believe she eloped! How romantic!

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.900
It's hardly credible, but...

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:59.560
"Love transcends family and status
to blaze at the ends of the Earth!"

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.730
Isn't that more exciting to you girls?

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:02.900
You bet!

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.350
Listen up! Forget about burning people
and track down some burning hearts!

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.060
You got it, Chief!

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:16.190
{=4}Romeo and Juliet
Romeo: Defrott
Juliet: Chiyo Sanjo

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.350
It's changed to <i>Romeo and Juliet</i> .

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.810
I liked Misaki's Salomé better.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:24.770
That which we call a rose,
by any other name would smell as sweet.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.190
Romeo?!

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:37.440
Did you like Misaki, miss?

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.310
Why did Misaki leave?

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:42.100
Did she really elope? With whom?

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:45.020
Who are you, miss?

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.100
Aoi Shirase for the Nitto News.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.560
Oh, that paper that prints such
an amusing mix of fact and fiction.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:51.470
Nitto News
Screen Actress's Illicit Affair

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.100
But I want to write the truth!

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:58.350
The truth of human combustion,
and of the elopement!

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.810
Is that all?

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.440
I'm looking for someone.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:06.190
A childhood friend who never
came back from Siberia.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:09.270
He promised me that he wouldn't die.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.060
I wish I could die.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:17.980
No chance. Drink up.

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:19.810
Do I really have to?

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.020
Of course you do.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:25.350
This stuff's all we can eat or drink now.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:29.440
You won't die if you don't,
but you'll shrivel up like rotten fish.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.850
I hate rotten fish.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.810
Pretend it's turtle blood, and it'll be fine.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:38.020
I don't like eating turtle much, either.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.150
Just give in already.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.270
We're not human anymore.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:45.150
We're Japan's vampire unit now.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:48.190
That means we're vampires!

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:50.900
But we're still just like humans, right?

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:55.480
We'll probably die if we get shot, won't we?

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.900
Care to test that theory?

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:00.480
Ow! That hurts!

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.310
St-Stop that!

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.270
Yamagami!

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:06.520
See? He's fine.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:09.270
Aren't vampires incredible?

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.520
Takeuchi! Stop horsing around!

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:14.270
Why not? It's not hurting anything.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:19.980
Just about any injury you receive
will heal if you just ingest blood.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.810
A rare A class probably has more
sensitive senses of taste and smell.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:26.850
Unlike an unranked.

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:30.400
Well, excuse me for being unranked.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:33.100
This is candy made from blood.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:37.190
I developed it for emergencies,
but why not try one?

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.730
I hear our commander's making an appearance.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:48.520
He's back from his convalescence then?

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:50.940
No one's met him yet, right?

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.560
What'll he be like?

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.190
Probably some kid fresh out of Ichigaya.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:57.730
I'll beat him into shape.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:59.940
I am Colonel Yoshinobu Maeda.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:04.060
Under my command, Code Zero
will operate as a vampire unit

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:08.190
and utilize vampire abilities to conduct
intelligence and special missions.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:13.480
We will find vampires hiding in Tokyo
who may indiscriminately attack humans,

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:17.190
then capture or dispose of them.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:18.730
What is it, Yamagami?

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.060
Is there something on my face?

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.980
Why you, of all people?

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.650
That's Colonel Maeda, unranked.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:26.690
Why?!

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:29.100
We were at Ichigaya together.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.270
And yet I outstripped you in rank,

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:34.810
and Lance Corporal Kurusu
outstripped you in vampire ranks.

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:36.230
How ironic.

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.480
Maeda!

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:38.730
Maeda?

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.770
Colonel Maeda.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.850
Very good, <i>Major</i> Yamagami.

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:48.310
Nabeshima bumpkin.

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:50.310
Shutaro Kurusu.

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:54.310
Our nation's one and only A class,
bitten by an S class.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:55.980
You don't look it.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.770
I agree, sir.

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:02.310
But you're the least human
of us all, aren't you?

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:06.190
I'll have you make full use
of your abilities in battle.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:07.440
Battle, sir?

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:11.270
When a vampire's bodily fluids
enter a human body,

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:15.060
nine out of ten can't resist it
and die of poisoning.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:16.310
Poisoning?

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:19.150
So, we were lucky then?

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.690
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.940
The issue is those who survive
and become vampires.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.730
They have a need to ingest blood.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:31.560
Of course, they won't starve to death
quickly like a human would,

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:37.940
but their instinctive craving
for blood should intensify instead.

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:42.020
Enough talk. Who should I kill?

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:45.350
Reports of human combustion
are currently on the rise.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:50.190
That means that vampires in hiding
have been exposed to sunlight.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:53.270
Until recently, there were
only a few cases a year.

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:55.230
Now, seven in the past month.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:57.940
Then the one at Tokyo Station makes eight.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:01.600
Special Forces Unit 16 will narrow
it down from those eight locations.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:06.650
Hopefully, humans will be able
to find vampires in hiding.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.230
Umm, may I?

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:14.770
Most people bitten by vampires
should die of poisoning, right?

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:17.190
Why aren't their bodies being found?

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:23.150
Someone may be either supplying
them with blood or hiding the bodies.

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:25.520
Places that deal in blood?

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.480
Butchers, hospitals...

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.810
And that place.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.460
TENMANYA

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.100
I haven't been playing lately.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.270
You can play organ?

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:05.230
What do you take me for?

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.020
Please don't touch that.

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:12.310
It's old and therefore fragile.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.900
I believe Mr. Takeuchi sent you?

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:31.400
That's right. He said we
could get information here.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:34.520
You can, here at the Tenmanya.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:37.310
From daytime to nighttime customers.

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:41.350
Information that people like you desire.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.650
Are you a vampire, too?

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:45.770
No, look closely; he's human.

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:48.520
A human is helping vampires?

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:50.480
It would make a long story.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:51.690
We don't need it.

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:55.980
We want to know how vampires are getting blood.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.100
You mean blood-sellers?

00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.900
What are they?

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:03.060
They quite literally sell blood.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:08.980
They deal in blood for transfusions,
with sodium citrate to prevent coagulation.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:12.440
Until now, we had a monopoly and
made arrangements for our customers.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:16.690
How? Do you know where the vampires hide out?

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.060
I don't, and I wouldn't tell you if I did.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:19.900
What?!

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:22.520
Yamagami, he's a child.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:27.270
A merchant who sells
his customers has no future.

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:31.230
That's one thing the Tenmanya will never do.

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:32.480
However,

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:37.150
a rival dealer has recently
appeared from another quarter.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:39.310
I suppose I could sell them.

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:40.810
Who?

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:43.650
I don't know that much, but...

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:47.230
What is that?

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.810
This is business, so...

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.980
I'm joking.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:54.980
I'd just like you to crush my business rival.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.600
Head clerk, bring it to us.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:01.980
Thank you.

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:08.940
Here you are.

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:09.940
What is it?

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:14.730
A bootleg of our product
and a tool of our business rival.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.600
Oh, you mustn't, Masakichi...

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.900
Just leave it to me.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.480
Well, Onatsu? How's "Ascra"?

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:37.060
You're so naughty.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.600
You wanna go on another eating spree?

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:42.100
We'll have no place to call home again.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.100
I know that, but...

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.440
...but...

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.560
...that's enough of that!

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.600
Okay, fine.

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:55.350
Listen, let's live somewhere,
just the two of us.

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:58.730
Like Okaru and Kanpei in that kabuki play.

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:01.850
Huh? Don't they die in the end?

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:05.940
You're so adorable.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:15.270
Fire!

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:24.270
What do you think?
They're the cream of the army.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.440
Useless.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:26.150
What?

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:29.400
We're fighting vampires.
A Type 38 won't stop them.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:31.810
Look into improving our firepower.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:35.400
Stock up on hand grenades
and Type 3 machine guns if possible.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:36.730
Sir, we're in the city.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.190
Will we be fighting tanks?

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:39.940
It would be easier if we were.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:42.350
Tanks are large, slow-moving targets.

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:45.060
Vampires can disappear right in front of you.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:46.350
That's why

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:48.900
it will come down to these.

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:52.440
If they can't do it, they'll either
die or become vampires.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:56.060
Drag them into the sunlight before that happens.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:59.020
Assemble the men. Find their caskets.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.060
Yes, sir!

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:12.900
Always search in pairs.

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:16.150
Avoid independent action.
Don't enter shadows unprepared.

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:18.150
We are eyes and ears.

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:23.480
Our purpose is to use our hands and feet
to find what we're looking for.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:25.850
What we're looking for is garbage!

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:28.440
Don't overlook a single speck of it!

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.150
That's all! Dismissed!

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:31.310
Yes, sir!

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:51.600
Mr. Policeman!

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:52.850
Oh, the reporter.

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:54.730
I'm Aoi Shirase.

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:58.150
Are you investigating the human combustion case?

00:14:58.150 --> 00:15:01.190
People bursting into flame? That's impossible.

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:04.600
I believe it can happen.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:08.400
You certainly cling to your ideas.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.980
Shutaro used to tell me that all the time.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:12.940
Shutaro?

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.730
My childhood friend.

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:19.690
He's supposed to be in the army,
but he was reported dead recently.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.940
I see.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.100
Are those for your lover?

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:25.940
No.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:28.900
Then why are you leaving flowers?

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:32.440
I couldn't keep my word. That's all.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:39.230
Asters mean "I'll never forget you."

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:43.440
I knew it; he did lose his lover.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:01.770
May I...?

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.350
Oh, help yourself.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:09.310
I'm learning your habits, Colonel.

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:10.850
Did you find the trash?

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:12.520
Yes.

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:14.020
Where?

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:16.270
A Kayabacho tenement house.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.020
Seal the bridges and streets at midnight.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.560
We'll mobilize Zero.

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:22.730
Yes, sir.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.270
Thank you very much.

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:25.440
You're welcome.

00:16:30.310 --> 00:16:33.270
Will this be the last time I see it?

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:34.940
Or...?

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:42.350
The encirclement is complete.

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.650
But will this work?

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:46.520
There's a gap on the Hamacho side.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:48.730
I left it open on purpose. Let's go.

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:49.730
Yes, sir.

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.690
All residents are evacuated.

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:01.520
Good work.

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:17.150
A pair!

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:20.060
Let's go!

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.600
A vampire couple, huh?

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:29.600
Not a winning combination.

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:35.900
Damn those bastards!

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:36.900
Stop.

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:38.900
It's just ten or 20 humans.

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:40.560
It's what we've always done!

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.480
I have a bad feeling.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:46.770
Is my older, centenarian wife
sharing the wisdom of her years?

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:49.730
No, I'm worried about you.

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:52.440
Since you bought that stuff
from Yokohama, you've been...

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:53.560
Shove it!

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:55.900
I'm sick of living in hiding!

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.440
I said stop!

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.480
There's no going back now.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:09.150
They're after us now, and they'll
split us up if we get caught.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:10.650
Shh!

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.310
We're surrounded. This way.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:20.650
They won't let us pass!

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:22.060
Ram them and make them.

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:23.850
That's a cabinet minister's car!

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:26.730
I'll take responsibility. Do it!

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:31.520
Are you really all right, dear?

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:32.770
Be quiet!

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:34.440
They really showed up.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:37.440
Maeda really knows his stuff.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:39.980
Hey, who's gonna do it?

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:42.850
Excuse me... You're vampires, right?

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:44.150
Get out of our way, kid!

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:45.850
Stop it, dear!

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.310
He's... dangerous.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:50.060
This kid? How?

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.520
What should I say?

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:55.360
Can't you even tell that much anymore?

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:57.520
Would you please surrender
and come with us, if you don't mind?

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:05.850
Vampires, there are two roads open to you!

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:06.810
One!

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:12.100
Obey us, Special Forces Unit 16,
and you will receive blood and registrations!

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:13.100
Two!

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:17.350
Refuse to obey, and we will end
your bloodlines here and now!

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:18.400
Fire!

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.520
Damn you!

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:30.850
Makin' a fool of m--

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.730
Dear...

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:59.060
Umm, please surrender.

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:02.190
Let us live, Kanpei.

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:03.400
Kanpei?

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:07.400
It looks like the play has come true.

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:18.600
So, she's the parent root.

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:19.850
Kurusu!

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:24.150
Vampires,

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:27.900
there are two roads open to you.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:31.270
So, it's time for love, and blossoms, to fall.

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:43.400
But you

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:45.100
don't get a choice!

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:58.020
Now, will he die of poisoning,
or become one of us?

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.520
It's anyone's guess.

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:10.400
Moriyama, leave the rest to me.

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:14.900
Colonel...

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:28.230
Aww. And he was a valuable sample, too.

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:04.810
I should be the only one to become a monster.

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:47.030
His Dream
